From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] rockchip: rk3399: nova: Step 2, our own TPL, SPL and
 BL31 before this U-Boot proper

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

A third build of the Rigol DHO800/DHO900 and MHO900 board,
nova-mainline.config merged over nova-<family>-rk3399_defconfig: the
card's whole boot chain from source. TPL (the LPDDR4 init,
rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-100.dtsi) and SPL go to card LBA 64 as
idbloader.img, this U-Boot proper with TF-A's BL31 and the control DT to
LBA 2048 as u-boot.itb, in the zero gap before vendor storage, never at
the default 0x4000 (the scope's uboot partition). The Maskrom images
(ROCKCHIP_MASKROM_IMAGE) run the same chain from RAM.

It is the chainload's U-Boot proper, with the same board file, ladder
and FIT path: the I-cache, the MMU and the D-cache on before the device
model's scan (BL31 enters it uncached, as the stock U-Boot entered the
chainload: board_f 0.65 s -> 0.03 s there), the LZ4 FIT held to its
header's length and crc32, the attempt record in PMUGRF OS_REG1, the
watchdog, the silent console recorded into the pmsg zone. What the stock
U-Boot did before it started the chainload is done here
(nova_stock.{c,h}, pure logic a host program builds alone):

- the reboot flag in PMUGRF OS_REG0, read in board_early_init_f: low
  byte 1 and 0x1888aaff are Loader mode, 3 boots recovery first, 6 and 7
  (the stock "wipe data") and everything else a normal boot;
- on a normal boot, Run/Stop at power-on: SPL opens the front panel's
  UART0 (1,500,000 baud, GPIO2_C0/C1 only) before it loads U-Boot and
  records when, so every frame from then on waits in the receive FIFO;
  U-Boot reads them all and listens on until NOVA_RUNSTOP_WINDOW_MS
  (50 ms, the stock window) after the open, a deadline, not a fixed wait
  of its own. A press or release (FA 08 0C 34 AF, FA 08 00 58 AF)
  anywhere in the stream is Loader mode; otherwise the power-on-mode
  frame FA 05 05 0A AF (auto) goes to the panel;
- the card's PARM must be the committed table (NOVA_PARM_BYTES,
  NOVA_PARM_CRC32), or Loader mode; its CMDLINE is the stock loader's,
  the parameter partition first on a recovery boot;
- on a normal boot the misc message at misc + 16 KiB (only there:
  boot-recovery starts at recovery); nothing writes misc;
- boot, recovery, backup in the stock order: Rigol's Android from a KRNL
  container (the ramdisk from that partition, the kernel from kernel,
  rk-kernel.dtb from resource); a plain NovaOS image held to its id; a
  chain image by the ladder, with the watchdog armed right there, where
  the stock U-Boot would have started the chainloaded one, so the same
  span of the boot runs under it in both steps. Every reset the ladder
  makes comes back to this stock order, which reads the flag it left as
  the stock U-Boot does;
- Loader mode: Rockusb on OTG0, the rear USB device port, no timeout.

No OP-TEE runs: the DRAM banks keep the region the chainload cuts out.
The kernel's command line is built here as the stock U-Boot builds it,
without its logo word (no logo is drawn).

TPL honors BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD in OS_REG0 (ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG), and
U-Boot proper never writes it (ROCKCHIP_DOWNLOAD_KEY off). TPL, SPL and
BL31 are quiet (no banners, no DRAM report, BL31 at its errors-only log
level). TPL's and SPL's bootstage records are stashed at 0x1f0000 and
U-Boot proper puts them, with its own, in the kernel's /bootstage, so a
boot shows every stage's time; SPL's record of UART0's open sits beside
them at 0x1f1000. Both are in the free RAM below 2 MiB: above the first
MiB, which BL31 makes secure, and the ramoops area, and below U-Boot's
and Linux's RAM.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
